  "instructions": "Use relevant memories or search_memory; current instructions win. When save_memory is available, honor explicit requests to remember. Otherwise save only what would guide a separate future session: the user's stated standing preferences, habits, corrections or conventions, or architectural reasons the repo cannot reveal. Skip one-off requests, plan approvals, styling and local implementation choices, progress, and facts available in code, Git or project docs. Never save secrets."
